# The Dockerfile copies three scripts and nothing else. Excluding everything
# and allowing those back is deliberate: a blacklist would need updating every
# time a file appears next to the launcher, and the one file that must never
# reach the daemon - .env.local - would be one forgotten line away from being
# sent. Denying by default also keeps .git out of the build context.
*

!entrypoint.sh
!init-firewall.sh
!agent-identity.sh
